1
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:06,500
Proposition forty-two restricts certain future taxes.

2
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:10,700
It focuses on owning personal property, including financial assets,

3
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:13,320
and on taxes applied retroactively.

4
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:17,600
Personal property here generally means assets other than real

5
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:18,100
estate.

6
00:00:19,460 --> 00:00:23,000
California already taxes income from assets, such as investment

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,360
gains, and some forms of personal property already have

8
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:26,660
taxes.

9
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:30,280
It generally does not tax simply owning stocks.

10
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:34,320
The proposal is primarily about restricting new taxes, not

11
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:35,420
issuing a refund.

12
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:39,820
Imagine a business owner reviewing the value of company

13
00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:40,200
assets.

14
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:44,440
Owning equipment or shares is different from earning a

15
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:44,760
profit.

16
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,480
A rule against a new ownership tax does not,

17
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:52,280
by itself, eliminate income taxes on profits or every

18
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:54,260
tax the owner already pays.

19
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:58,420
A budget analyst considers future options for raising revenue.

20
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:02,620
The measure would prohibit new state taxes on ownership

21
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,440
of financial assets and other personal property.

22
00:01:06,220 --> 00:01:10,220
It also limits certain retroactive taxes: taxes applied to

23
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:13,020
activities or periods before the tax was adopted.

24
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:17,140
For illustration, a tax enacted later but applied to

25
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:20,000
income earned in an earlier period is retroactive.

26
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:24,020
The measure’s detailed rules determine what is prohibited; this

27
00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:27,940
is not a claim that every tax adjustment becomes

28
00:01:27,940 --> 00:01:28,600
impossible.

29
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:32,160
The analyst does not attach a specific dollar saving

30
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:32,820
or loss.

31
00:01:33,180 --> 00:01:36,620
Future revenue might rise less because some tax options

32
00:01:36,620 --> 00:01:37,640
